    "# 49 - Milestone Project: Missing-Data Interpolation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Section:** FNN Milestone Projects | **Prereqs:** `FNN Milestone Projects/FNN_Adding Machine.ipynb` | **Next:** `Weight Initialization/WeightMatrixSizeExplanation.ipynb`\n",
    "\n",
    "Reframing imputation as supervised learning: delete 10 values of `residual_sugar`\n",
    "at random, train a regressor on the rows that still have it, and predict the\n",
    "missing ones. This is exactly how model-based imputation works in practice\n",
    "(sklearn's `IterativeImputer` does the same thing with a simpler estimator).\n",
    "\n",
    "**When it is worth it.** Mean or median imputation is the default and is often\n",
    "enough. A model beats it only when the missing column is genuinely predictable\n",
    "from the others - which, as `Metaparameters/CodeChallenge_PredictSugar.ipynb`\n",
    "showed with the correlation matrix, is *not* true for residual sugar. Expect\n",
    "mediocre predictions, and treat that as the finding.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The pipeline is the part to copy:** the 10 held-out rows are removed before\n",
    "anything else, the scaler is fit on the training split alone, and the device is\n",
    "chosen with a `cuda.is_available()` check rather than hardcoded."
   ]
  },
